-- The Time of Science COSMOS chain (client localization)
-- +migrate Up

UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='My research is going well. My decision to hire independent pilots has paid off really well. But I fear it might also have backfired somewhat by putting too much heat on me. The Sisters have become aware of my whereabouts and what I''m trying to achieve. While I doubt it, one of my rivals could decide to dent my efforts my sending some thugs here to rough me up and destroy my work. The physical risk does not concern me all that much, but if I lose my work I have nothing.
I always like to be on the safe side, so I''ve made backup copies of my research. I need to get them to a safe place. First, I considered placing them in a depository box in a bank, but me hiring such a box is too easy to track down. Maybe I''m being paranoid, but you never know. So instead I''ve opted to hire a low-key storage room in a remote system to stash my backup copies in.
Obviously, I can''t go there myself, I might be followed. But they would never bother with someone such as you, so you''re an ideal candidate for the job. Take my stash to the Ragnarg system and by the time you return I''m sure I will have something more interesting, less paranoid, for you to do.' WHERE missionID=93481 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');
UPDATE missionObjectives SET briefingText='Thanks to you my research is back on track. I feel like I''m getting close to something big. You remember those tablets you got me awhile ago? I''ve managed to get some sense out of them and the information I''ve gleaned points to one place in particular that might hold the key to this whole thing. Unfortunately, that place is not exactly accessible. It lies deeper in the same complex that you found the tablets in, in the Traun system. This place I''m talking about is an ancient portal of some sorts. Sadly, it has long since ceased to function. I''m also beginning to suspect that it wasn''t built by the Nefantars themselves, but some other, more elusive, civilization. I''m not sure exactly where it lies, but it is an immense structure, so it can''t be all that hard to locate.
I need pieces of the damaged portal. If you can get them for me I would be eternally grateful. Just to show you how serious I am, I''m offering you a very rare BPC as a reward when you return with a few pieces of the damaged portal. Needless to say, you can expect trouble there, so be prepared.' WHERE missionID=93482 AND (briefingText IS NULL OR briefingText='');

-- +migrate Down
-- (briefings stay)
